  "summary": "Tabots carried to water in velvet and brocade: January Epiphany re-baptizes a nation in song.",
  "description": "Timkat (January 19) celebrates Christ's baptism: each church's tabot — the tablet symbolizing the Ark — is wrapped in brocade, hoisted on a priest's head beneath velvet canopies, and carried in drum-throbbing procession to a blessed pool or river. Crowds in white shemma cotton camp overnight in prayer; at dawn the water is blessed and the crowd leaps in, renewing baptism vows. Lalibela's rock-hewn basins and Gondar's Fasilides Bath stage the grandest Timkat, UNESCO-listed since 2019.",
